; Leg KP -- HW_TEST_16aq Part 3, THE BAD LINE.  Arm A: the Victor runs
; "CKBULK --nobulk --nodisplay".  Bulk arm OFF -- the control for KN.
;
; THIS IS THE LEG THE 10-FOOT CABLE WRAPPED AROUND MAINS WIRING IS FOR, and
; the framing changed once the preprocessor was consulted, so read this
; before running it.
;
; THERE IS NO LENGTH FIELD IN PLAY.  ckvictor.h defines NOPARSEN, which
; suppresses PARSENSE, which is what would have given length-driven packet
; reading -- so this build reads a packet by scanning for eol and nothing
; else.  The arm's memchr(src, eol, n) therefore looks for EXACTLY the byte
; the byte loop looks for, on exactly the same stream.
;
; SO THE PREDICTION IS THAT CORRUPTION MAKES NO DIFFERENCE BETWEEN THE ARMS.
; A mangled or lost terminator makes BOTH run to max-1 or to the alarm,
; identically, because neither is reading a length.  There is no fast-resync
; path in one arm and not the other; that only existed in the PARSENSE
; version of ttinl(), which this build does not compile.
;
; A NULL RESULT HERE IS A REAL RESULT.  It closes the one thing
; v9k/proofs/vttinl.c cannot reach -- real corruption, arriving at real
; timing, through the real chip -- and it should be written up as a finding,
; not as "nothing happened".
;
; WHAT WOULD FALSIFY IT: KP taking materially more TIMEOUTS than its pair,
; or KP not byte-exact where its pair is.  Either means the arm's recovery
; differs from the byte loop's, and the proof's equivalence claim needs
; re-examining against whatever the line actually did.
;
; RUN KN AND KP BACK TO BACK UNDER THE SAME NOISE -- same cable routing, same
; appliances running -- and WRITE DOWN WHAT THE NOISE ACTUALLY WAS.  Noise is
; not reproducible between sittings, so ONLY the KN/KP comparison means
; anything.  NEITHER LEG IS COMPARABLE TO KA-KD, and neither belongs in the
; cost figures.
;
; READ, PER LEG: md5, rxlost, rxfull, host timeouts, host retransmissions,
; the <crunched:...> lines in the packet log, and bulk n.  Note that rxlost
; counts INTERRUPTS THAT FOUND THE OVERRUN BIT, not bytes (SS16q), so one
; hold-off losing fifty bytes raises it by one.
;
; Decision rule 1 still applies: check "v9k: bulk sel= n=" in STEPKP.OUT
; first.  This arm must show sel=0 and n = 0.
;
; The binary is CKBULK.EXE, 226,330 bytes, md5 a9fa6b5c...

set speed 38400
set receive timeout 20
set parity none
set prefixing cautious
set block 3
log packets s16aqKP.pkt
send rcvkp.dat
statistics
